  "reason": "The current best evidence is RNA-only with scVI_n200 in single-profile form, which outperforms the RNA PCA baseline and the image-only ResNet baseline. The major untested design question is whether multiprofile aggregation can improve the strongest RNA representation. config_005 keeps the promising scVI_n200 encoder and adds only the simplest multiprofile aggregation, avgpool, making it a focused test of profile setting/aggregation without introducing a new encoder, image modality, transformer complexity, or fusion. This is an efficient use of the next experiment because it exploits the best known direction while clarifying whether multiprofile modeling is worth pursuing before moving to more complex multimodal configurations."
}

